faqs:
  - question: Can my PIP award go down if I challenge it?
    answer: >-
      It can. When a decision is looked at again, the whole award can be
      reviewed, so it could go up, stay the same or go down. This is rare, but
      it is worth getting advice first if you already get an award you are
      happy with in part.
  - question: What if I missed the one month deadline?
    answer: >-
      You can still ask, up to 13 months after the decision, but you must
      explain why you were late, for example because you were ill. Do it as
      soon as you can.
